{:edb/db-before-t 2693 :edb/db-after-t 2694 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536006 50 #inst "2026-10-09T12:45:39.162Z" 13194139536006 true] [17592186119735 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379173 13194139536006 true] [17592186119735 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379193 13194139536006 true] [17592186119776 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379166 13194139536006 true] [17592186119776 1020 #edb/ref 17592186379186 13194139536006 true] [17592186120442 1017 #edb/ref 17592186119127 13194139536006 false] [17592186120442 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379180 13194139536006 true] [17592186120442 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536006 true] [17592186120442 1100 "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b ∈ Col(E)$.\nIn the affirmative case, find the value of $x_{1} \\cdot x_{2} \\cdot x_{3} \\cdot x_{4}$, where $x_{1}$, $x_{2}$, $x_{3}$, and $x_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b = x_{1}e_{1} + x_{2}e_{2} + x_{3}e_{3} + x_{4}e_{4}$, and $e_{1}$, $e_{2}$, $e_{3}$, and $e_{4}$ are respective columns of $E$.\n\n$E = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139536006 false] [17592186120442 1100 "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139536006 true] [17592186120442 1145 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\text{ }0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=2 \\\\ 0=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379166 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379167 13194139536006 true] [17592186379166 1089 "q-110974" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379166 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536006 true] [17592186379166 1100 "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379166 1113 #uuid "c5aa2130-3437-5b23-b921-671ec9c0b0ed" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379166 1145 "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k-2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 0=k-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-10,$ which means that $k=10.$" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379168 13194139536006 true] [17592186379167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379169 13194139536006 true] [17592186379167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379170 13194139536006 true] [17592186379167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379171 13194139536006 true] [17592186379167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379172 13194139536006 true] [17592186379167 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536006 true] [17592186379167 1041 "selection" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379167 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379170 13194139536006 true] [17592186379167 1110 #uuid "903b870b-9442-58e1-a837-1bde2f59340b" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379168 1034 "-15" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536006 true] [17592186379168 1111 #uuid "72fd3cc6-fee5-5249-b60d-a672a32adb6b" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379169 1034 "28" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536006 true] [17592186379169 1111 #uuid "cc3626d4-1d1f-5ad1-b0b5-e62fc52f4b1f" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379170 1034 "10" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536006 true] [17592186379170 1111 #uuid "ccdb75c0-2295-5bbe-ae11-f0cae2afd0f0" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379171 1034 "6" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379171 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536006 true] [17592186379171 1111 #uuid "7760b649-f606-5f12-a086-ad38f1b32a12" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379172 1034 "-4" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379172 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536006 true] [17592186379172 1111 #uuid "91e137ae-fe57-51ad-a368-cca4f25f01ea" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379173 1017 #edb/ref 17592186379174 13194139536006 true] [17592186379173 1089 "q-111050" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379173 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536006 true] [17592186379173 1100 "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379173 1113 #uuid "a7d73384-0a7c-5be0-8c8c-14e2cdf3bb45" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379173 1145 "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{4}=-2 \\\\ 0=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=2.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379175 13194139536006 true] [17592186379174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379176 13194139536006 true] [17592186379174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379177 13194139536006 true] [17592186379174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379178 13194139536006 true] [17592186379174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186379179 13194139536006 true] [17592186379174 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536006 true] [17592186379174 1041 "selection" 13194139536006 true] [17592186379174 1104 #edb/ref 17592186379175 13194139536006 true] [17592186379174 1110 #uuid "8979069e-acc9-5e1e-bbb9-4e01bc953da7" 13194139536006 true] [